            <h2>Airlines Flying from Los Angeles to Hawaii</h2>
            <p>Six carriers operate nonstop service between LAX and Honolulu: Hawaiian Airlines, Alaska Airlines, United, Delta, American, and Southwest.</p>
            <h3>Hawaiian Airlines</h3>
            <p>Hawaii's flagship carrier, part of the Alaska Air Group family since 2024 while keeping its own brand, delivers the most authentically island-flavored experience on the route.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstops to Honolulu plus direct service to Maui, Kona, and Lihue on Airbus A330 and Boeing 787 jets</li>
                <li>Complimentary island-inspired hot meals in economy, a rarity on US domestic routes</li>
                <li>Free high-speed Wi-Fi across the transpacific fleet</li>
                <li>Earning through the shared Atmos Rewards program with Alaska Airlines</li>
                <li>Genuine Hawaiian hospitality in language, music, and crew culture</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Alaska Airlines</h3>
            <p>The West Coast's hometown carrier brings deep Hawaii expertise and a top-tier loyalty program.</p>
            <p><b>Highlights:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstops to Honolulu, Maui, Kona, and Lihue aboard Boeing 737 MAX aircraft</li>
                <li>Atmos Rewards earning with valuable elite status and partner redemptions</li>
                <li>Complimentary elite upgrades when available, plus premium extra legroom</li>
                <li>Seamless connections from dozens of West Coast cities through LAX</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>United Airlines</h3>
            <p>United links its LAX operation to Hawaii with mainline aircraft and a massive onward network.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstops to Honolulu, with seasonal neighbor-island frequencies, on Boeing aircraft</li>
                <li>MileagePlus earning with Premier qualifying credits toward elite status</li>
                <li>Economy Plus extra legroom and occasional lie-flat Polaris seats on widebody rotations</li>
                <li>Terminal 7 and 8 convenience with United Club access for members</li>
                <li>Star Alliance connectivity for travelers continuing beyond Los Angeles</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Delta Air Lines</h3>
            <p>Delta leverages its modernized Terminal 3 hub at LAX to serve Honolulu with signature operational reliability.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily nonstop service to Honolulu with comfortable Boeing and Airbus mainline aircraft</li>
                <li>SkyMiles earning plus Medallion elite benefits and upgrade priority</li>
                <li>Free Wi-Fi for SkyMiles members on equipped aircraft</li>
                <li>Delta Sky Club access in Terminal 3 for eligible passengers</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>American Airlines</h3>
            <p>American connects LAX to the islands with broad schedules and the world's largest loyalty program.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Daily Honolulu nonstops plus service to Maui, Kona, and Lihue on many dates</li>
                <li>AAdvantage mileage earning with Loyalty Points toward elite status</li>
                <li>Main Cabin Extra legroom and premium cabins on select rotations</li>
                <li>Admirals Club and Flagship lounge access at Terminal 4</li>
                <li>Extensive domestic feed enabling single-ticket itineraries from across the country</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Southwest Airlines (Low-Cost)</h3>
            <p>Southwest brings its value-driven model to Hawaii with an interisland network that makes island hopping easy.</p>
            <p><b>Features:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Multiple daily nonstops between LAX and Honolulu aboard Boeing 737 MAX 8 aircraft</li>
                <li>Rapid Rewards points with no blackout dates and fully refundable flexibility.</li>
                <li>Newly assigned seating with extra-legroom options introduced across the fleet</li>
                <li>Checked bag fees now apply on most fares; free bags remain for top elites and premium tickets.</li>
                <li>Easy add-on interisland hops on a single ticket</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Connecting Options</h3>
            <p>One-stop itineraries route through San Francisco, Oakland, San Jose, San Diego, Sacramento, and Phoenix, often priced below nonstops. Hawaiian's interisland hubs can also turn a one-stop journey into a two-island trip on one fare.</p>
            <h2>Seasonal Variations</h2>
            <h3>Peak Season: Mid-December through March, June through August</h3>
            <p>The islands' two high seasons combine winter escape travel with summer family vacations.</p>
            <p><b>During peak months:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Airfares reach annual highs, with June and July averaging the year's most expensive round trips</li>
                <li>Christmas through New Year's commands the steepest premiums of the calendar</li>
                <li>Humpback whale season from December through April draws wildlife travelers to Maui and the Big Island</li>
                <li>Resort rates climb with minimum-stay requirements; rental cars and luaus book out weeks ahead</li>
                <li>Spring break weeks in March and April create secondary fare spikes</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Shoulder Season: Mid-April through Early June, September through Mid-December</h3>
            <p>The sweet spot for value, weather, and space.</p>
            <p><b>Advantages:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Economy fares typically run 20 to 30 percent below peak levels</li>
                <li>Warm, dry weather with calmer ocean conditions on south-facing shores</li>
                <li>Shorter lines at Pearl Harbor, Diamond Head, and Haleakala sunrise reservations</li>
                <li>Aloha Festivals in September and the Hawaii Food and Wine Festival in October</li>
                <li>Better upgrade availability and award seat inventory across all carriers</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Off-Peak Value Windows: Mid-January through February, Early December</h3>
            <p>Post-holiday weeks deliver the cheapest fares of the year.</p>
            <p><b>Benefits:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>February is historically the cheapest month, with round trips averaging near $328</li>
                <li>Hotel promotions and uncrowded resorts reward flexible travelers</li>
            </ul>
            <p><b>Considerations:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Winter is Hawaii's rainy season, especially on windward coasts; pack a light waterproof layer</li>
                <li>North Shore surf runs huge, thrilling to watch but dangerous for casual swimmers</li>
            </ul>
